  level:'A2', xp:100, duration:'15 min', topic:'Articles',
  sections:[
    { title:'No article needed!', content:'Sometimes we use NO article at all. This is called the **zero article (Ø)**. Use it with:\n• Plural countable nouns (general): **Dogs** are loyal. **Books** teach us.\n• Uncountable nouns (general): I love **music**. **Water** is essential.\n• Proper nouns: **London**, **Brazil**, **Maria**.\n• Meals: I have **breakfast** at 7. We eat **lunch** together.\n• Languages: She speaks **French** and **Arabic**.\n• Sports: He plays **football**.\n• School subjects: I study **mathematics**.\n• Illnesses: She has **diabetes**.' },
    { title:'The key distinction', content:'Compare:\n• "I love **the** music in this film" (specific) vs "I love **music**" (general)\n• "**The** water in this river is cold" (specific) vs "**Water** is a liquid" (general)\n• "She went to **school**" (the activity of studying) vs "She went to **the** school" (the building)\n• "He is in **hospital**" (British English - he is ill) vs "He is in **the** hospital" (visiting someone)' },
    { title:'Zero article examples', content:'• **Coffee** is my favourite drink. (general)\n• **Children** need love and care. (all children)\n• She studied **medicine** at **university**.\n• I play **tennis** on Sundays.\n• **France** is famous for its food.\n• He goes to **church** every Sunday.\n• They travel by **bus** every day.' },
  ],
