  level:'A2', xp:100, duration:'15 min', topic:'Vocabulary: Food',
  sections:[
    { title:'Food categories', content:'**Fruit:** apple, banana, orange, strawberry, grape, mango, pear, lemon.\n**Vegetables:** carrot, potato, tomato, onion, garlic, cucumber, lettuce, broccoli, pepper.\n**Meat and fish:** chicken, beef, pork, lamb, salmon, tuna, shrimp/prawns.\n**Dairy:** milk, cheese, butter, yoghurt, cream.\n**Carbs:** bread, rice, pasta, noodles, cereal.\n**Other:** egg, oil, sugar, salt, pepper (spice), flour, honey.' },
    { title:'Meals and drinks', content:'**Meals:** breakfast, lunch, dinner/supper, snack, dessert.\n**Cooking verbs:** boil, fry, bake, grill, roast, steam, chop, slice, mix, stir.\n**Drinks:** water, juice, tea, coffee, milk, beer, wine, fizzy drink/soda.\n**Describing food:** fresh, frozen, raw, cooked, spicy, sweet, sour, salty, bitter, mild, rich, light, heavy, greasy, healthy, organic.' },
    { title:'Examples in context', content:'• "I had **scrambled eggs** and **toast** for breakfast."\n• "She **boiled** the **pasta** for ten minutes."\n• "He loves **spicy** food - the **hotter**, the better."\n• "Can you **chop** the **onions** while I **fry** the **garlic**?"\n• "I am **vegetarian** - I do not eat **meat** or **fish**."' },
  ],
